WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.030
One verse of the Qur'an,
Surah 4, verse 34.

2
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.930
Two English translations.

3
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.110
One says men are the protectors
and maintainers of women.

4
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.280
The other says men are in charge of women.

5
00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:16.820
Yet Muslims believe men and
women come from one soul,

6
00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.940
with the same reward for faith.

7
00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:22.170
So if one verse seems to
put husbands in charge,

8
00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:25.190
how have Muslim women
scholars read it differently?

9
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.300
In this mission, you'll
weigh the key Arabic words,

10
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:31.850
and see how classical scholars
hedged the verse with limits.

11
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.420
Then you'll meet an
American Muslim scholar,

12
00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:37.250
Amina Wadud, and test what she found.

13
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.990
Your mission: find out how Muslim women
scholars have read this verse anew,

14
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:43.230
and weigh their case.
